From 2ab379f8de339f5d4c0f6ee6e72d6a54bb3eea1c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Nguyen <the.nguyen.yf@renesas.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 06:25:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] [renesas noup] platform: ra: Add RA8M2/RA8P1 and
 ML-DSA-87 support

Add Renesas downstream support for the RA8M2 and RA8P1 platforms,
including ML-DSA-87 (PQC) boot image validation. These changes are
not upstream in TF-M.

Platform (platform/ext/target/renesas/ra):
- Add common RA core, RA8M2 and RA8P1 SoC support and the
  EK-RA8M2 / EK-RA8P1 (CM85) boards
- Add CMSIS MRAM flash driver and SCI_B UART driver
- Enable BL2 (MCUboot) and the Platform partition by default
- Add TF-M mailbox / multi-core support for a remote CM33 NSPE

ML-DSA-87 (PQC) boot image validation:
- Add ML-DSA-87 support to MCUboot (lib/ext/mcuboot/0002 patch) and
  TF-PSA-Crypto (lib/ext/tf-psa-crypto/0018 patch)
- Add MCUBOOT_SIGNATURE_TYPE=ML-DSA-87 handling to BL2, the thin PSA
  crypto core and provisioning, with support for an external
  mldsa-native dependency
- Add ML-DSA-87 root keys and the dilithium-py tool requirement
- Check that CRYPTO_STACK_SIZE is large enough for ML-DSA-87

Common:
- Bump MCUBOOT_VERSION from v2.4.0 to v2.5.0 and refresh the
  bootutil key ID patch
- Pass --keep-cr to git am so patches with CRLF line endings (FSP)
  apply cleanly

Signed-off-by: The Nguyen <the.nguyen.yf@renesas.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
